        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/delta_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rich soils in the Yazoo-Mississippi Delta support Delta City's agricultural economy, which focuses on cotton, soybeans, and rice.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/delta_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Delta City sits on a flat alluvial plain with elevations generally between ninety and one hundred thirty feet above sea level.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/delta_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The landscape around Delta City features deep clayey soils that often experience seasonal cracking and slow water permeability.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/delta_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Undisturbed zones near Delta City contain bottomland hardwood forests with oak, hickory, and cypress trees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/delta_mississippi"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Delta City experiences a humid subtropical climate with hot, humid summers and mild winters.",
